# Leak-guard denylist (template) — copy to `.leakcheck`, which is gitignored.
#
# internal/leakcheck scans the repo (tracked + untracked-but-not-ignored files) for these
# tokens (case-insensitive, literal) and fails the build if any appears. Kube
# context/cluster/namespace names and cloud account IDs are derived automatically from your
# kubeconfig — list here only what a kubeconfig can't surface: internal PRODUCT and SERVICE
# names that show up in dogfooding notes (a real workload name, an internal middleware, a
# private cluster nickname). One-off extras can also be passed via KSYNC_LEAKCHECK_EXTRA.
#
# One token per line; '#' starts a comment. Keep this .example free of any real name.
#
# my-internal-product
# some-private-service
# 111122223333
